INSERT INTO `questions` VALUES (478,NULL,NULL,8,'BULK_CSV',1,'Mock 1',2,'Azure',23,'DP-900: Microsoft Azure Data Fundamentals','Mock 1','Q1. A retail company is evaluating structured and unstructured data for customer insights. Which statement accurately describes the primary difference relevant to analytics?','Azure Synapse Analytics for integrated analytics and warehousing.','Azure Data Factory for ETL and orchestration.','Azure Databricks for big data processing and machine learning.','Azure SQL Database for transactional relational workloads.','Azure Cosmos DB for globally distributed NoSQL storage.','Azure Monitor for telemetry and observability.','multiple_choice','A,F','Select two answers that together form the managed solution meeting the described requirements. Each selected service provides complementary functionality.','Other choices are partially correct but miss key requirements from the scenario.','Core Data Concepts','Core Data Concepts Fundamentals','Scenario-based','3',1,0,'core_data_concepts','N/A','N/A',1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,6,2,'Active',NULL,NULL,'307d36f070facf1ec59d0f97d0a616c3fe8d854770b6cf32047ce7ee0631c34b',4,'2025-11-11 13:40:39',4,'2025-11-11 13:42:52'),(479,NULL,NULL,8,'BULK_CSV',2,'Mock 1',2,'Azure',23,'DP-900: Microsoft Azure Data Fundamentals','Mock 1','Q2. A SaaS provider needs a managed relational database with automatic backups, geo-replication, and predictable performance for transactional workloads. Which Azure service fits best?','Azure SQL Database — managed relational DB with automated backups and scaling.','Azure Cosmos DB — globally distributed multi-model NoSQL database.','Azure Blob Storage — object store for unstructured data.','Azure Synapse Analytics — analytics and data warehousing platform.','Azure Table Storage — key-value store for simple workloads.','On-premises SQL Server managed by customer.','single_choice','D','The selected option is the most appropriate managed Azure service for the stated requirement; other options may be plausible but don\'t fully satisfy the constraints.','Other choices are partially correct but miss key requirements from the scenario.','Relational Data on Azure','Relational Data on Azure Fundamentals','Scenario-based','3',1,0,'relational_data_on_azure','N/A','N/A',0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,6,1,'Active',NULL,NULL,'089607e4356b9427c9c0a369917cd3ce0feed1ff3b0c126cd8039dff7a69a9fa',4,'2025-11-11 13:40:39',4,'2025-11-11 15:00:36'),(480,NULL,NULL,8,'BULK_CSV',3,'Mock 1',2,'Azure',23,'DP-900: Microsoft Azure Data Fundamentals','Mock 1','Q3. A SaaS provider needs a managed relational database with automatic backups, geo-replication, and predictable performance for transactional workloads. Which Azure service fits best?','Azure SQL Database — managed relational DB with automated backups and scaling.','Azure Cosmos DB — globally distributed multi-model NoSQL database.','Azure Blob Storage — object store for unstructured data.','Azure Synapse Analytics — analytics and data warehousing platform.','Azure Table Storage — key-value store for simple workloads.','On-premises SQL Server managed by customer.','single_choice','B','The selected option is the most appropriate managed Azure service for the stated requirement; other options may be plausible but don\'t fully satisfy the constraints.','Other choices are partially correct but miss key requirements from the scenario.','Relational Data on Azure','Relational Data on Azure Fundamentals','Scenario-based','4',1,0,'relational_data_on_azure','N/A','N/A',1,0,'https://lmsimage.blob.core.windows.net/cmsimages/certification-thumbnails/azure_dp_900__microsoft_azure_data_fundamentals_banner.webp','https://lmsimage.blob.core.windows.net/cmsimages/certification-thumbnails/azure_dp_900__microsoft_azure_data_fundamentals_banner.webp','https://lmsimage.blob.core.windows.net/cmsimages/certification-thumbnails/azure_dp_900__microsoft_azure_data_fundamentals_banner.webp','https://lms